      "prompt": "Our replenishment dashboards display dense, data-heavy tables for grocery store managers. How do you ensure that complex, dynamic data grids remain accessible to screen reader users, and which specific WCAG criteria do you prioritize when building these types of interfaces?",
      "answer_outline": "The candidate should mention using semantic HTML (like table headers and scope attributes) and ARIA live regions for dynamic updates. They should reference WCAG success criteria like 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships) or 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value) to demonstrate practical application.",
      "difficulty": 2
